</figure>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Replay Experiment</span>. To further show the effectiveness of CP in ATTA, we allow the compared methods access to the labeled calibration set as replay data during adaptation. Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Annotation-Efficient Active Test-Time Adaptation with Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> reports results on PACS. While SimATTA with replay improves accuracy on domain <span id="S3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A</span>, CPATTA achieves superior performance on the other two domains and obtains the best overall real-time and post-adaptation accuracy. This confirms that leveraging the calibration set through CP is more effective than using it as replay data.</p>
</div>
